  "checkpoints": "The 12 final latest.zip files pinned by the hashes in config/campaign-room2-heldout-ab-200.json, re-verified 2026-09-23. The clone is a descriptive reference, labelled biased on these starts because it was fitted on 5 of the 7 routes (check routes 20260922-164006 and 20260922-164552).",
  "evaluation_protocol": {
    "evaluation_seed": 20260924,
    "canonical_stochastic_episodes": 50,
    "deterministic_repeats_per_start": 2,
    "stochastic_episodes_per_demonstration_start": 5,
    "episodes_per_checkpoint": 556,
    "play_order": "canonical start first, then demonstration starts in dataset trajectory order and prefix order; at each start all stochastic episodes, then all deterministic repeats",
    "episode_deadline_frames": 1800,
    "success": "episode ending equals success",
    "repeat_justification": "50 canonical episodes give a standard error of at most 7 points for one checkpoint's canonical rate. 5 per demonstration start give about 40 to 75 stochastic episodes per route cluster (8 to 15 starts), a route-level standard error of at most about 8 points; the primary summary then averages 7 routes and 12 checkpoints. Deterministic play should repeat exactly because the game is deterministic; 2 repeats only confirm that."
  },
  "analysis": {
    "label": "diagnostic only; not a confirmatory A/B claim; does not change the published Room 2 result",
    "determinism_rule": "If a start's two deterministic repeats disagree, report it as a validity problem, use the mean of the two repeats for that start, and state how many starts were affected. Never silently use only the first repeat.",
    "primary": "Per checkpoint, over the 42 demonstration starts whose start x is below 460: for each of the 7 route clusters, the mean over its primary starts of (deterministic success, averaged over the 2 repeats) minus (stochastic success rate out of 5); then the equal-weight mean of the 7 route values. Route 20260922-164111 has only 4 primary starts (counts 6, 9, 6, 4, 6, 5, 6). Starts from one route are adjacent prefixes and never independent; the route is the cluster.",
    "canonical_start": "Reported separately per checkpoint: deterministic success (mean of 2 repeats) minus stochastic success out of 50.",
    "summary_over_checkpoints": "The checkpoint is the unit: all 12 values, their median and range, and the count of checkpoints at least +10 points and below +3 points. Arms A and B are also summarised separately, descriptively.",
    "secondary_descriptive": [
      "the same difference over all 72 demonstration starts, route clusters weighted equally",
      "failures by end_x band (last frame with a player): before 360, 360 to 459, after 459, per checkpoint and mode",
      "failures by true max_x band (running maximum over the episode), the same bands, labelled separately",
      "ending counts per mode",
      "clone reference row, labelled biased on these starts"
    ],
    "analysis_code": {
      "script": "scripts/analyze_noise_check.py",
      "sha256": "b6a5074bc9d777a2844c5a10e067c09bc0268d1606d3d077d81d3e1c93056f66",
      "git_blob": "a17a5bd63adcdbe47af218b0e200bed8403ec8d8",
      "commit": "85bb8ed2da93f84acce2c0036daf0b0c7cab1c20",
      "note": "Committed before any run. The sha256 is of the file as committed; with line-ending conversion the git blob id is the stable identity. Run with --output to a new path."
    },
    "primary_start_x_below": 460,
    "primary_starts": 42,
    "start_x_definition": "A start's x is its recorded world position x in the start list (starts.json), the expected arrival position checked by the environment."
  },
  "decision_rule": {
    "written_before_data": true,
    "rule": "Applied to the primary (the 42 starts before x 460). If the primary deterministic-minus-stochastic difference is at least +10 points in at least 9 of the 12 checkpoints, recommend that the next experiment predeclares its evaluation mode and treats the fine-tuning entropy setting as a training-design question, ahead of O1. If it is below +3 points in at least 9 of the 12, noise is not the main cost: recommend O1 or O2. Otherwise the check is inconclusive and makes no recommendation. Deterministic play can also be worse, which is why the rule is two-sided. The clone never counts. The owner makes the final call.",
    "scope": "This check can support a recommendation about the evaluation mode. It cannot show that a lower entropy bonus during training would produce a better policy. That needs a new training experiment.",
    "no_retroactive_change": "Switching the published Room 2 metric to deterministic play after the fact is ruled out; any adoption goes into a new predeclared experiment.",
    "thresholds": {
      "favour_points": 10,
      "favour_min_checkpoints": 9,
      "null_points": 3,
      "null_min_checkpoints": 9
    },
    "outcomes": {
      "favour": "recommend predeclaring the evaluation mode in the next experiment, ahead of O1; the training entropy setting stays a separate training-design question",
      "null": "noise is not the main cost: recommend O1 or O2",
      "inconclusive": "this check makes no recommendation"
    }
  },
  "public_claims": "None without a separate owner decision.",
  "budget": {
    "episodes": 7228,
    "estimate": "About 1 to 1.5 s per episode: the Room 2 held-out campaign took 166 to 297 s per 200 episodes including launch. Every episode here also replays a 326 to 886 frame start recipe, and canonical-start episodes play the whole room, up to 1,800 frames on a timeout. About 10 to 15 minutes per checkpoint, about 2 to 3 hours for all 13.",
    "limit_minutes_per_run": 90,
    "limit_reason": "A policy that often times out costs roughly 5 to 7 s per 1,800-frame episode plus its start replay, the clone especially, and a run that hits its limit is a failed run."
  },
  "machinery": "scripts/run_overnight.py with this committed plan: clean tree, pinned runtime, dry run first, one live game script at a time, Steam running, laptop on the charger.",
