  "field_meanings": "In these rows max_x is the true running maximum of world x and end_x the position on the last frame that had a player. In evaluate_heldout.py rows, max_x and end_x are the final frame's x. The two end_x values agree whenever the final frame has a player.",
  "amendments": [
    {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "before_any_data": true,
      "number": 1,
      "change": "Primary restricted to the 42 demonstration starts with start x below 460; all 72 kept as secondary.",
      "reason": "The 30 starts after x 459 are likely at ceiling in both modes: held-out states 300 or more frames into the room scored 93% to 100% per run in both arms. They would pull every checkpoint's difference towards 0."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "before_any_data": true,
      "number": 2,
      "change": "Added the start_replay_failure rule: stop, amend, re-commit, restart every checkpoint.",
      "reason": "Start validity does not depend on the policy, so a partial campaign is never analysed."
    },
    {
      "date": "2026-09-23",
      "before_any_data": true,
      "number": 3,
      "change": "limit_minutes raised from 45 to 90 for every run.",
      "reason": "A mostly timing-out policy (the clone especially) could exceed 45 minutes, and a timed-out run fails."
    },
